## 📌 About This Repository

This repository contains a collection of **40 Python-based cryptography experiments** developed as part of the **CSA5123 — Cryptography** course/laboratory work.

The repository is intended to provide practical exposure to cryptographic concepts by implementing algorithms and security-related techniques using Python.

Rather than focusing only on theoretical concepts, these experiments provide hands-on experience with the logic behind encryption, decryption, classical cryptographic techniques, and computational approaches to information security.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

The primary objectives of this repository are to:

- Understand fundamental concepts of cryptography
- Implement cryptographic techniques using Python
- Explore encryption and decryption processes
- Understand how cryptographic algorithms transform information
- Develop practical programming skills in cybersecurity
- Analyze the logic behind classical cryptographic methods
- Gain experience implementing security-related algorithms
- Strengthen problem-solving skills through practical experimentation

---

## 🧠 Key Concepts

The experiments in this repository provide practical exposure to areas such as:

- 🔐 Encryption
- 🔓 Decryption
- 🔑 Cryptographic keys
- 🧮 Mathematical transformations
- 🔤 Classical cipher techniques
- 🛡️ Information security
- 💻 Python-based cryptographic programming
- 🔎 Algorithmic analysis
- 🔄 Reversible transformations

> **Note:** The exact concepts covered by each experiment are represented directly in the corresponding Python source file.

